# Codegraph (local CLI only)

Use the local `codegraph` CLI (v1.6.0, on fnm PATH) as the **only** code-intelligence source in this project.

The managed `user-codegraph` MCP endpoint is unreachable (returns `permission_denied 403` from the China proxy on the managed remote URL). It is not configured here - both `~/.cursor/mcp.json` and `./.cursor/mcp.json` have an empty `mcpServers: {}`. Do **not** add it back, and do **not** try `codegraph install --target cursor` again - it spawns a redundant managed entry that 403s.

## Primary command

```bash
codegraph explore "<query>" --path /home/tuantm/projects/tmcs
```

- Accepts a natural-language question or a bag of symbol/file names.
- Returns verbatim, line-numbered source grouped by file, plus the call path and a blast-radius summary.
- Treat the returned source as already Read - do **not** re-Read those files.

## Other commands

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `codegraph query <search>` | Search for symbols |
| `codegraph node <name>` | One symbol's source + caller/callee trail, or read a file with line numbers |
| `codegraph callers <symbol>` | All functions that call a symbol |
| `codegraph callees <symbol>` | All functions a symbol calls |
| `codegraph impact <symbol>` | What code is affected by changing a symbol |
| `codegraph files` | Project file structure from the index |
| `codegraph status` | Index status and statistics |

## When to use

BEFORE reading files to understand code, before editing a function/symbol, when investigating a bug or a flow, when surveying an area, when asked "how does X work" or "where is X defined".

## Anti-patterns

- Do **not** grep + Read to reconstruct what `codegraph explore` returns in one call.
- Do **not** run `codegraph init` yourself - indexing is the user's decision. If a project is unindexed, fall back to built-in tools and mention the user can run `codegraph init`.
- Do **not** call the managed `user-codegraph` MCP namespace - it is unauthorized in this workspace.

## Staleness

Index lags writes by ~1s. A tool response starting with `⚠️ Some files referenced below were edited since the last index sync…` names the files to re-Read. Files **not** in that banner are fresh - still trust codegraph.

## Working directory

Always pass `--path /home/tuantm/projects/tmcs` (or `--path "$PWD"` after `cd`-ing into the repo) so it picks up the existing `.codegraph/` index.
